Compatibility with bsl-language-server
--------------------------------------
Where this project reports the same diagnostics as bsl-language-server,
the agreement is deliberate. Rule codes, tags, severities, default
activation and the places a rule fires form an interface that existing
SonarQube quality profiles and CI pipelines depend on; a tool that
reported different rules under different names on the same code would
not replace its predecessor. These values match that project's published
rule documentation, which is where they can be checked.

This is a statement about observable behaviour, not about source code:
implementing the same interface independently is intended, and copying
implementation text is not.

